data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261018175545451518255c955d568CA2uOijp","created":1792346145,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1a74ce124a314d3584d3c724","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"file_edit","arguments":"{\"new_string\":\"5. **Freeze on issuance:** sources lock once point + band are issued; later fetches are verification-only and labeled as such.\\n\\n### Correction to S3 (partial-day subtlety)\\nAt cutoff 17:48:51 UTC = 18:48 BST, the Oct 18 local day is still in progress → S3 = **complete** days Oct 15–17 + **partial** Oct 18 (00:00–17:48 UTC only). No input may contain any target-day (Oct 19) data. Same rule applies in backtest: the d-1 full daily mean is NOT knowable at an 17:48 UTC cutoff on d-1, so the persistence baseline uses d-2 complete day or partial d-1.\\n\\n### Backtest protocol (design only — nothing run yet)\\n- **Scheme:** rolling-origin walk-forward, one pseudo-forecast per target date d in evaluation window (~90 days), cutoff_c = 17:48 UTC on d-1 (mirrors live protocol).\\n- **Availability standard (strict):** each date's inputs = only content *accessible* by cutoff_c — NWP cycles initialized ≤ cutoff_c (12Z and earlier; exclude same-day 18Z), obs through cutoff_c, **vintage-matched** climatology (1981–2010 normals for pre-2021 dates, 1991–2020 after — never today's normals retro-applied).\\n- **Frozen recipe:** point rule + band rule identical at every date; any re-tuning is walk-forward (parameters at date d chosen from data strictly before d) or nested (train/eval split). No post-hoc metric shopping.\\n- **Verification:** fixed in advance, one source, same station/definition for all dates; scored only after all pseudo-forecasts generated (scoring never feeds back into inputs).\\n- **Hazards controlled:** reanalysis-as-predictor (ERA5 is not a real-time-available input — excluded as predictor, allowed only as final verification), dataset revisions (prefer